d83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T19:28:24-08:00","id":1185806,"title":"","content":"Native americans have served as american or canadian soldiers afield since at least World War II, who's to say some globe-trotting homid or kinfolk did not leave chilldren unknowingly in distant shores through the decades since?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T20:58:22-08:00","id":1185821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185680#post1185680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The opening comic was him and a few other ocean oriented Garou - at least one Glasswalker and I can't remember the others off the top of my head and don't have the book handy - out off the coast of Australia (I want to say all or most of them were RAAustralia characters) trying to make contact with Rokea. Unfortunately, they succeed. The Wendigo guy is, IIRC, the last one left alive, and you don't actually see him die, but from the way the last panel looked, if he lived they need to change his deed name to Luckiest Son of a Bitch on Two Legs. Personally, I like to think he made it, but I've always been a bit of a Pollyanna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers for an ST's portion of a 17 year old book!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The adventure module in the same book confirms that he made it back to shore by using Sky Running, but he had a Qyrling in his head, too.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-14-2018, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T21:22:55-08:00","id":1185826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185806#post1185806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Native americans have served as american or canadian soldiers afield since at least World War II, who's to say some globe-trotting homid or kinfolk did not leave chilldren unknowingly in distant shores through the decades since?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THis too, as I said before spirits will claim theirown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T02:20:38-08:00","id":1185857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185648#post1185648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So No Tribes functionally exist except the Bonegnawers and Glasswalkers right?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185665#post1185665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wendigo could travel to other places. One of my favorite Wendigo NPCs was the surfer guy in Rage Across Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, a Wendigo can travel. Doesn't mean that his grand children, when raised in Australia for two generations, with no exposure to Wendigo culture would still be considered Wendigo kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Liam is exaggerating my original post with his comment. But he is right, there is a reason why the Bone Gnawers are second in numbers only to the BSD, and why the Wendigo are all but extinct. It's exactly this point.<br /> <br /> The struggle for cultural identity is a huge topic for native Americans and a lot of other groups that are embedded in other larger groups. That said, I find it was the wrong move, from revised edition onward to downplay this aspect in favor of a Out-of-.game more political correct tolerance.<br /> <br /> And yes, this in consequence means, that a white person shouldn't play a Wendigo in LARP. Is this a unfair restriction? I don't think so, it is life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T03:41:05-08:00","id":1185869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185826#post1185826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> THis too, as I said before spirits will claim theirown.</div> </div> </div> </div>What may lead to interesting situations for a lone Wendigo - or family, in those cases with two generations or more between them - of mixed stock whose main connection to its native american heritage/tribal identity comes through their totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:08:49-08:00","id":1185881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185869#post1185869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What may lead to interesting situations for a lone Wendigo - or family, in those cases with two generations or more between them - of mixed stock whose main connection to its native american heritage/tribal identity comes through their totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which leads to a number of different situations and points of view on the matter.<br /> <br /> For Evan, it was necessary to prove himself several times, because even when one Wendigo sept and their Elders accepted him as Wendigo, other still needed their own proof. An Elder Theurge in of the tribe novels, iirc, stated, that spirits have a multitude of opinions and agendas and that he wouldn't have risen to Elder rank, if he wouldn't make up his own mind over things, instead of taking anything a spirit states as fact. If that extends to Tribal Totem Avatars ? Well, hopefully, for they aren't without fail.<br /> <br /> Also, ancestry wasn't the only requirement, for that his ancestors had Wendigo among them was (I'd guess) easily proofed, once it was discovered.<br /> <br /> Obviously, they accept someone into the tribe with the Rite of Passage. But it is still up to the garou to make up the quest for the Rite, and judge whether or not it was successful. That, in general, doesn't mean, that the garou is a paragon of tribal virtues. Because, there are still tribe members that defect to become Ronin, to become members of other tribes, to be become BSD. Also there are breakers of the Litany and cowards and what not. And, while the tribal totem would have accepted them into the tribe at some point, the tribal totem also allows the tribe to cast members out with specific rites.<br /> <br /> So, this in consequence means, that &quot;the spirits claim their own&quot; is not an absolute. It is more like and endorsement of sorts, aimed at the tribe, who are the ones to decide whether or not a garou gets accepted or not. And this can mean, that one sept accepts you as a Wendigo, and one other does not extend this position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:30:53-08:00","id":1185887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185881#post1185881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leads to a number of different situations and points of view on the matter.<br /> <br /> For Evan, it was necessary to prove himself several times, because even when one Wendigo sept and their Elders accepted him as Wendigo, other still needed their own proof. An Elder Theurge in of the tribe novels, iirc, stated, that spirits have a multitude of opinions and agendas and that he wouldn't have risen to Elder rank, if he wouldn't make up his own mind over things, instead of taking anything a spirit states as fact. If that extends to Tribal Totem Avatars ? Well, hopefully, for they aren't without fail.<br /> <br /> Also, ancestry wasn't the only requirement, for that his ancestors had Wendigo among them was (I'd guess) easily proofed, once it was discovered.<br /> <br /> Obviously, they accept someone into the tribe with the Rite of Passage. But it is still up to the garou to make up the quest for the Rite, and judge whether or not it was successful. That, in general, doesn't mean, that the garou is a paragon of tribal virtues. Because, there are still tribe members that defect to become Ronin, to become members of other tribes, to be become BSD. Also there are breakers of the Litany and cowards and what not. And, while the tribal totem would have accepted them into the tribe at some point, the tribal totem also allows the tribe to cast members out with specific rites.<br /> <br /> So, this in consequence means, that &quot;the spirits claim their own&quot; is not an absolute. It is more like and endorsement of sorts, aimed at the tribe, who are the ones to decide whether or not a garou gets accepted or not. And this can mean, that one sept accepts you as a Wendigo, and one other does not extend this position.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, far from saying it is - my interest was more on the strangeness of the situation of someone who's both closer to native american stock than Evan (less than a century of separation) and yet more isolated (born and grown in another continent), with only the totem's inhuman perspective as gateway into its garou heritage. That should lead to peculiar results, at least without some interaction/visitation to nnattive Wendigo through moon bridges or other forms of contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2018, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:54:34-08:00","id":1185895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185857#post1185857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, a Wendigo can travel. Doesn't mean that his grand children, when raised in Australia for two generations, with no exposure to Wendigo culture would still be considered Wendigo kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Liam is exaggerating my original post with his comment. But he is right, there is a reason why the Bone Gnawers are second in numbers only to the BSD, and why the Wendigo are all but extinct. It's exactly this point.<br /> <br /> The struggle for cultural identity is a huge topic for native Americans and a lot of other groups that are embedded in other larger groups. That said, I find it was the wrong move, from revised edition onward to downplay this aspect in favor of a Out-of-.game more political correct tolerance.<br /> <br /> And yes, this in consequence means, that a white person shouldn't play a Wendigo in LARP. Is this a unfair restriction? I don't think so, it is life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, Wendigo and to a lesser extent the Uktena actually have subculture keeping things active, and Stargazers should be crazy active. If you can show me something equivalent for Silver Fangs, Shadowlords, Black Furies or children of Gaia. Conversely Hakken should be the real tribe vs Shadowlords.<br /> <br /> Fianna have an active culture, Get kind of do. Glasswalkers seem to solidly have something as do Bonegnawers.<br /> <br /> And obviously silent striders should be completely extinct thanks to Set.<br /> <br /> <br /> And HOW do Red Talons work in your setup at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:03:42-08:00","id":1185897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185887#post1185887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, far from saying it is - my interest was more on the strangeness of the situation of someone who's both closer to native american stock than Evan (less than a century of separation) and yet more isolated (born and grown in another continent), with only the totem's inhuman perspective as gateway into its garou heritage. That should lead to peculiar results, at least without some interaction/visitation to nnattive Wendigo through moon bridges or other forms of contact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would argue, that such a person can't be/become a Wendigo.<br /> Without proper education (even with constant contact with the tribal totem avatar, it hardly is proper), and without garou performing a porper Wendigo Rite of Passage, the garou would, in my opinion, not be a Wendigo. Then, I also would think, that Wendigo would take such a person, and bring him/her, possible against her will, to a Wendigo sept to be educated. Members of other tribes would also try to contact the Wendigo an make that happen.<br /> <br /> However, if that for some reason wasn't happening, it might be the start of something new. I mean, if a group of people still had Grandfahter Thunder as their totem, and contact to him, but were otherwise separated from their brethren and their culture, they might create something like, well the Hakken. But, there just seems to be a critical number of garou for this to work. A single person being brought up with only spirits as advisers would certainly be something unique - but like Evan, wouldn't be accepted right away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:17:22-08:00","id":1185899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185895#post1185895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Wendigo and to a lesser extent the Uktena actually have subculture keeping things active, and Stargazers should be crazy active. If you can show me something equivalent for Silver Fangs, Shadowlords, Black Furies or children of Gaia. Conversely Hakken should be the real tribe vs Shadowlords.<br /> <br /> Fianna have an active culture, Get kind of do. Glasswalkers seem to solidly have something as do Bonegnawers.<br /> <br /> And obviously silent striders should be completely extinct thanks to Set.<br /> <br /> And HOW do Red Talons work in your setup at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we misreading each other?<br /> <br /> You say all this tribes have an active culture. I agree, and I further postulate, that you must be part of that culture to be part of the tribe.<br /> <br /> So, where is the problem with the Red Talons or any tribe for that matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:33:19-08:00","id":1185903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185899#post1185899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we misreading each other?<br /> <br /> You say all this tribes have an active culture. I agree, and I further postulate, that you must be part of that culture to be part of the tribe.<br /> <br /> So, where is the problem with the Red Talons or any tribe for that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no external culture for Red Talons, SIlver Fangs, Shadowlord, Children of Gaia, Black Furies and the Silent Striders culture was actively destroyed by Set. By your logic over half the tribes should be worse off than Wendigo. And the Three most common should be Bongnawers, Glasswalkers, and Stargazers. This doesn't match anything close to a reading of the books.<br /> <br /> IF we are going to accept &quot;super sekrit&quot; cultures.. the idea that Wendigo who have actual real active living culture vs hidden ones would be &quot;nearly extinct, is still kind of absurd, yes there aren't that many Native americans but more of them are closer to Wendigo culture than your average white person is to any tribe(Except potentially bonegnawer and glasswalker) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:49:32-08:00","id":1185909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185897#post1185897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would argue, that such a person can't be/become a Wendigo.<br /> Without proper education (even with constant contact with the tribal totem avatar, it hardly is proper), and without garou performing a porper Wendigo Rite of Passage, the garou would, in my opinion, not be a Wendigo. Then, I also would think, that Wendigo would take such a person, and bring him/her, possible against her will, to a Wendigo sept to be educated. Members of other tribes would also try to contact the Wendigo an make that happen.<br /> <br /> However, if that for some reason wasn't happening, it might be the start of something new. I mean, if a group of people still had Grandfahter Thunder as their totem, and contact to him, but were otherwise separated from their brethren and their culture, they might create something like, well the Hakken. But, there just seems to be a critical number of garou for this to work. A single person being brought up with only spirits as advisers would certainly be something unique - but like Evan, wouldn't be accepted right away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more interested in the proccess and potential results, strange and &quot;flawed&quot; though they may be and potential drama resulting from interaction than any sense of &quot;propriety&quot; on what defines a tribe or not, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:10:50-08:00","id":1185916,"title":"","content":"Personally I think think the Wendigo should span out across the Americas to protect more indigenous peoples as a whole. They feel the Uktena are neglecting Native peoples in South and Central America for their expansion to become a more global animist tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:10:57-08:00","id":1185917,"title":"","content":"So this is my take and I'm wondering if anyone else feels the same on why a European Wendigo feels off:<br /> <br /> For me what makes a Euro-Wendigo feel off is due to my own experience with the &quot;blonde in buck skin&quot; cliche that is common in so much of Hollywood and I've seen in gaming circles (so much cringe from the old white wolf java sites). I've run into people using images like Brad Pitt for their Wendigos. Its felt super common for me where people want to play someone with Native ancestry but don't want to have dark skin. So while I understand everyone's points about LARPers wanting go avoid engaging in &quot;red face&quot;, for me it feels wrong to inject Europeans into the Wendigo (note, I have no issue with Siberian people's being Wendigo however.) <br /> <br /> Instead I always viewed the Uktena to be a tribe that was more about indigenous people in general (after all they did take in the Australian Aborigines) vs the Wendigo's hard more traditionalist Siberian/Canadian/northern US. <br /> <br /> As a side note I do no there isn't really 1 way native people look. My Family is a mix of Irish, Seneca, Italian and Mohawk and I've grown up getting odd looks about my family (you can see the mental pundit squares) since some of us look more European while others much more Native","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:45:51-08:00","id":1185931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185903#post1185903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no external culture for Red Talons, SIlver Fangs, Shadowlord, Children of Gaia, Black Furies and the Silent Striders culture was actively destroyed by Set. By your logic over half the tribes should be worse off than Wendigo. And the Three most common should be Bongnawers, Glasswalkers, and Stargazers. This doesn't match anything close to a reading of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;extrenal&quot; you mean a human culture the tribal culture borrowed from more or less, like viking for Get of Fenris or celts for Fianna, then the answer is, that there doesn't need to be one.<br /> Kinfolk of any tribe has a culture that is adjacent to the tribal culture and they strife to protect it more or less vehemently. Red Talon Kin being all animals are a bit off, but one could all their drive to live &quot;wild&quot; versus in captivity a &quot;culture&quot; of sort.<br /> <br /> So, my logic doesn't need an external culture for the kinfolk or tribe to bloom. My statement only was, that if any individual kin or local group of kin would cease to practice their culture but be assimilated into a non-garou culture, they would loose their kinfolk status. Therefore it makes it unlikely that group of Wendigo settled in Poland and stayed Wendigo over an extended period of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185903#post1185903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF we are going to accept &quot;super sekrit&quot; cultures.. the idea that Wendigo who have actual real active living culture vs hidden ones would be &quot;nearly extinct, is still kind of absurd, yes there aren't that many Native americans but more of them are closer to Wendigo culture than your average white person is to any tribe(Except potentially bonegnawer and glasswalker)</div> </div> </div> </div>The average white person, who isn't close to any tribe is (per definition) no kinfolk. The ratio of kinfolk to non-kinfolk humans among native Americans is most likely higher than among the general population. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185909#post1185909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested in the proccess and potential results, strange and &quot;flawed&quot; though they may be and potential drama resulting from interaction than any sense of &quot;propriety&quot; on what defines a tribe or not, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would think that this person would be an outsider among his people. Every meeting with an NPC would be in part a process to win him over and gain acceptance. This could be a mere social situation, but could also require that the character has to proof and re-proof himself as Wendigo, for example by performing tests and tasks that the local sept requires from cubs, or young-cliaths, like showing his skill in areas valued by Wendigo, like survival, hunting, endurance and so on...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:48:09-08:00","id":1185932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185916#post1185916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think think the Wendigo should span out across the Americas to protect more indigenous peoples as a whole. They feel the Uktena are neglecting Native peoples in South and Central America for their expansion to become a more global animist tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the Uktena are the tribe who are/would/should integrate south american or Central American natives. If the authors failed to mention that in newer books than this is unfortunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T07:15:54-08:00","id":1185941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185917#post1185917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is my take and I'm wondering if anyone else feels the same on why a European Wendigo feels off:<br /> <br /> For me what makes a Euro-Wendigo feel off is due to my own experience with the &quot;blonde in buck skin&quot; cliche that is common in so much of Hollywood and I've seen in gaming circles (so much cringe from the old white wolf java sites). I've run into people using images like Brad Pitt for their Wendigos. Its felt super common for me where people want to play someone with Native ancestry but don't want to have dark skin. So while I understand everyone's points about LARPers wanting go avoid engaging in &quot;red face&quot;, for me it feels wrong to inject Europeans into the Wendigo (note, I have no issue with Siberian people's being Wendigo however.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and for those outside USA and Canada, the culture can be amazingly hard to figure out and find anything about. Nevermind figuring out minuscule details.<br /> <br /> Then, as a personal issue, face blindness is a pain when you try to make a character look like they are from a specific first nations culture like this fellow;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/vDDYxn3.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/vDDYxn3.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/vDDYxn3.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.imgur.com/vDDYxn3.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Leucistic due to me wanting to explore what Wendigo pb5 WOULD look like in a person. Inuit and Yup'ik mix from Yukon, at least I tried to make him look it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-14-2018, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T07:18:33-08:00","id":1185943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185931#post1185931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;extrenal&quot; you mean a human culture the tribal culture borrowed from more or less, like viking for Get of Fenris or celts for Fianna, then the answer is, that there doesn't need to be one.<br /> Kinfolk of any tribe has a culture that is adjacent to the tribal culture and they strife to protect it more or less vehemently. Red Talon Kin being all animals are a bit off, but one could all their drive to live &quot;wild&quot; versus in captivity a &quot;culture&quot; of sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>If culture can be completely hidden and have no wider human culture to exist off of why are Wendigo &quot;almost extinct&quot; why can't they have large secret bastions all over the damned place?<br /> <br /> <br /> So, my logic doesn't need an external culture for the kinfolk or tribe to bloom. My statement only was, that if any individual kin or local group of kin would cease to practice their culture but be assimilated into a non-garou culture, they would loose their kinfolk status. Therefore it makes it unlikely that group of Wendigo settled in Poland and stayed Wendigo over an extended period of time.[/quote]<br /> <br /> And why would they be more prone to do so in Poland? If they are a culture set appart that they do in secret that has real tangible supernatural capacity why would they assimilate.. ever?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The average white person, who isn't close to any tribe is (per definition) no kinfolk. The ratio of kinfolk to non-kinfolk humans among native Americans is most likely higher than among the general population. </div> </div> </div>One would assume that a sufficiently large culture would have an external footprint, you seem to have no issue with completely hidden and secret ones though.<br /> <br /> I'm still going to question how Silent striders exist in your world at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T08:19:09-08:00","id":1185960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185943#post1185943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If culture can be completely hidden and have no wider human culture to exist off of why are Wendigo &quot;almost extinct&quot; why can't they have large secret bastions all over the damned place?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the simple answer is, that the books say, they are.<br /> <br /> The longer answer would be, that, yes, there could be, in theory, native Americans who secretly migrated to Africa, maintained secretly their worship of a Ice Spirit and hid that fact from the world. <br /> <br /> The question is, if you want that in your game world. I wouldn't. I see the drama and appeal of the Setting where the Wendigo as a people were to proud to go into hiding and therefore were murdered. It is closer to real live and therefore their struggle for survival as a culture is more worthwhile as a game topic.<br /> <br /> If just anybody who feels the Wendigo ideals are cool, or who has only the slightest amount of native american blood but no regard for their culture could actually become a Wendigo, then their struggle, and by extension their existence in the Setting as a whole, would be pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185943#post1185943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why would they be more prone to do so in Poland? If they are a culture set apart that they do in secret that has real tangible supernatural capacity why would they assimilate.. ever?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between the Wendigo and Uktena, compared to the Western tribes is that they did never go into hiding. Possibly now would be the time, but that is another topic.<br /> <br /> The other tribes moved into hiding with the rise of the Church and the Inquisition. The older Dark Age Werewolf stated, that the Veil was added to the Litany at this point in time. Even if you don't believe that part, the general population in Europe by that time is estimated to be around 100 million people. So, probably not many of those kinfolk, therefore garou and their kin started hiding their &quot;pagan&quot; practices, or integrated them into Christianity.<br /> <br /> Uktena, Croatan and Wendigo on the other hand lived openly. Even if you assume that they had the Veil and hid their true selves from any non-kin native Americans, if their were any, they and their kin still weren't hunted for their believes until 500 or so years later. However, even then, the disease from Europe and Africa are the main reason for the death toll among native Americans in the early years. Wendigo, Croatan and Uktena couldn't have hidden their culture to prevent this.<br /> <br /> So, my take is, that the Wendigo and Uktena never started with hiding their culture from the general public and neither did their kinfolk. There was simply no point to it. They were persecuted and murdered for their skin color anyway. Uktena eventually opted to bring in other minorities (and their occasionally hidden cultural practices), Wendigo opted not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185943#post1185943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One would assume that a sufficiently large culture would have an external footprint, you seem to have no issue with completely hidden and secret ones though.<br /> <br /> I'm still going to question how Silent striders exist in your world at all.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, one would assume that a sufficiently large culture would leave signs of their existence. And possibly spawns of the Wyrm or Hunters try to find werewolf septs by searching for such a footprint. <br /> <br /> What do you mean by &quot;my world&quot;? What aspect of my statements is it, that you think is flawed?<br /> <br /> As for Silent Striders, they have a culture, it is based on a nomadic lifestyle, with plenty of kin that has settled, too. Their travels and (ir-)regular contact with others of their culture kept their culture alive and protected them from being assimilated into any other host culture. That is the benefit of traveling. People tend to not impose the same desire for conformity on a guest, then they do on the new neighbor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T08:25:38-08:00","id":1185962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185932#post1185932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the Uktena are the tribe who are/would/should integrate south american or Central American natives. If the authors failed to mention that in newer books than this is unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's just an option to show how they've also expanded their range like other tribes have, but still keeping with their theme. But yea, it seems a little odd, to say the least, to picture a Wendigo sept in say the Yucatan, but I could see them maybe taking kin among the Mapuche (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mapuche\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mapuche</a>) and other tribes that live in the Southern Cone of South America. It could also be very much a modern development since the Amazon War.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185917#post1185917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is my take and I'm wondering if anyone else feels the same on why a European Wendigo feels off:<br /> <br /> For me what makes a Euro-Wendigo feel off is due to my own experience with the &quot;blonde in buck skin&quot; cliche that is common in so much of Hollywood and I've seen in gaming circles (so much cringe from the old white wolf java sites). I've run into people using images like Brad Pitt for their Wendigos. Its felt super common for me where people want to play someone with Native ancestry but don't want to have dark skin. So while I understand everyone's points about LARPers wanting go avoid engaging in &quot;red face&quot;, for me it feels wrong to inject Europeans into the Wendigo (note, I have no issue with Siberian people's being Wendigo however.)<br /> <br /> Instead I always viewed the Uktena to be a tribe that was more about indigenous people in general (after all they did take in the Australian Aborigines) vs the Wendigo's hard more traditionalist Siberian/Canadian/northern US.<br /> <br /> As a side note I do no there isn't really 1 way native people look. My Family is a mix of Irish, Seneca, Italian and Mohawk and I've grown up getting odd looks about my family (you can see the mental pundit squares) since some of us look more European while others much more Native</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never been for the whole &quot;pure blooded Indian&quot; requirement from previous editions. I'm sure you know just as much as me the whole pure blood thing is very much a weird romanticization of the dominate culture in the States and kind of Canada, and something Natives who are largely on the assimilated side only put a lot of stock into. At the same time, there's not going to be much if any toleration for the one drop Cherokee princess trope of white folks dropping in to discover their lost heritage. They're going to keep kin among traditional circles, which might include some people who are heavily mixed with others, but Wendigo like Evan should be very much the exception to the rule.<br /> <br /> Basically, I can respect people who feel uncomfortable portraying a character from a culture they know very little about, but that doesn't excuse falling into the 'blonde in buckskin' cliche so you can make a Wendigo character. To be a part of the tribe, even if your character was born with blonde hair, is going to have a traditional indigenous culture be an important part of their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-14-2018, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T08:54:43-08:00","id":1185967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185962#post1185962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just an option to show how they've also expanded their range like other tribes have, but still keeping with their theme. But yea, it seems a little odd, to say the least, to picture a Wendigo sept in say the Yucatan, but I could see them maybe taking kin among the Mapuche (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mapuche\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mapuche</a>) and other tribes that live in the Southern Cone of South America. It could also be very much a modern development since the Amazon War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember some text, probably from revised TB, that the tribes spread to Central and South america was hindered by Bastet and human mages/sorcerers/priests. Now post-Inca, post-aztec and what not, they might have a good chance to spread there, and maybe they are in the process of doing so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T09:10:10-08:00","id":1185970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185967#post1185967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely remember some text, probably from revised TB, that the tribes spread to Central and South america was hindered by Bastet and human mages/sorcerers/priests. Now post-Inca, post-aztec and what not, they might have a good chance to spread there, and maybe they are in the process of doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, the Uktena were driven out of central and southern Mexico by the supernatural actors that rose with the Aztecs. I would still say they're an issue in a lot of places why the Uktena and Wendigo never had much of reach there up to today. Also, in my own head canon, there was something like the Beast Courts/Ahadi in the Americas, which also included defining the ranges of Werewolf territory. Lingering deals from that era played a part in one of my games. Just with the break down after colonization, I could see some expansion if you down play the dying race aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> However, in light of the Garou being a dying people, I guess it wouldn't make much sense outside of a few odd individuals that there would be South American Wendigo. If people wanted to despite this, it's not like Natives from down south haven't immigrated north, especially in the last few decades. So there's that for expanded kin range and also bringing Balam and Mokole farther north.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-14-2018, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T11:11:50-08:00","id":1186017,"title":"","content":"I'll try to explain my point about the Wendigo ethnicity thread, so sorry for my italienglish.<br /> <br /> Well, as full blood european ( for what I know) I feel a little bit ''cultural thief'' to play a character that is 100% native american ( or african or whatever) both outside than inside.<br /> Actually, I'm proud of my heritage, as every person should be, and it's exaclty because I highly respect every culture and ethnicity I know about, that I feel wrong to play a 100% ethnic wendigo. <br /> And that's why I would allow and I would play a ''white'' wendigo, for ''white'' ( or also black or whatever) I mean a wendigo with distant native ancestors: <br /> <br /> 1- Because I understand that someone can feel wrong, and feels that he's ''stealing'' culture.<br /> 2- Because actually, it's the totem that can allow you to join the tribe, even if your Native ancestor is four or five generations behind you.<br /> 3- I like to think about an ''eurosiberian'' culture of Wendigo that are able to cooperate with other tribes<br /> 4- I see no problems in a mature game to play a white or black wendigo that can have problem with his tribesmate because he looks everything but not native american.<br /> 5- Political Incorrectness is one of the best thing of werewolf. I like to face ethnic feuds with mature people during a game session.<br /> 6 - it's not because ''I don't want to have dark skin''. Actually, I feel wrong into play a dark skin character because, as I said, I feel that I'm disrespecting someone else cultural heritage to play something too far away from me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:06:04-08:00","id":1186034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185821#post1185821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoilers for an ST's portion of a 17 year old book!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The adventure module in the same book confirms that he made it back to sure by using Sky Running, but he had a Qyrling in his head, too.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. It's been so long I'd entirely forgotten about the adventure in the book. Thank you for reminding me. I'm going to have to go dig the Rokea book back out and reread it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:10:11-08:00","id":1186035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185903#post1185903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Silent Striders culture was actively destroyed by Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand what you mean by this statement. Can you please elaborate?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:34:13-08:00","id":1186039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185970#post1185970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yep, the Uktena were driven out of central and southern Mexico by the supernatural actors that rose with the Aztecs. I would still say they're an issue in a lot of places why the Uktena and Wendigo never had much of reach there up to today. Also, in my own head canon, there was something like the Beast Courts/Ahadi in the Americas, which also included defining the ranges of Werewolf territory. Lingering deals from that era played a part in one of my games. Just with the break down after colonization, I could see some expansion if you down play the dying race aspect of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My games have/had something similar, an ... I think alliance is too strong of a word, more like &quot;mutual understanding&quot;, between the Three Brothers, the Three Sisters (as I tend to refer to the American Bastet tribes), Nuwisha, and Gurahl, Corax, and Camazotz, and the more openminded Mokole. Sadly, it was badly crippled by the lost of the Croatan and all but lost in the second War of Rage, but started to make signs of a comeback in the 70s and 80s. <br /> <br /> As for South American Garou, there are a few mentions of native Uktena in Rage Across the Amazon and A World of Rage, IIRC, but not much else. I think the biggest issue is the lack of wolves in South America, but given the Uktena's propensity for learning secrets, I don't think it's that far fetched for them to have learned the secret of breeding with maned wolves (which is apparently not wolf, coyote, fox, dog or jackal, but it's own unique thing) the same way the Bunyip adapted to Australia and the one branch of Red Talons did to Southern Africa.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:52:32-08:00","id":1186047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1185962#post1185962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been for the whole &quot;pure blooded Indian&quot; requirement from previous editions. I'm sure you know just as much as me the whole pure blood thing is very much a weird romanticization of the dominate culture in the States and kind of Canada, and something Natives who are largely on the assimilated side only put a lot of stock into. At the same time, there's not going to be much if any toleration for the one drop Cherokee princess trope of white folks dropping in to discover their lost heritage. They're going to keep kin among traditional circles, which might include some people who are heavily mixed with others, but Wendigo like Evan should be very much the exception to the rule.<br /> <br /> Basically, I can respect people who feel uncomfortable portraying a character from a culture they know very little about, but that doesn't excuse falling into the 'blonde in buckskin' cliche so you can make a Wendigo character. To be a part of the tribe, even if your character was born with blonde hair, is going to have a traditional indigenous culture be an important part of their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying you can't have mixed race Wendigo who aren't Adam Beach look a likes. Like with my own family, I've grown up getting the odd looks when we introduce each other new people, and have been treated differently by people as well. For me being a Wendigo more about sticking tightly to both the Wendigo tribal culture as well as that of the kin culture you came from. Trying to maintain your people's identity despite all the hardships that both have faced. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186017#post1186017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll try to explain my point about the Wendigo ethnicity thread, so sorry for my italienglish.<br /> <br /> Well, as full blood european ( for what I know) I feel a little bit ''cultural thief'' to play a character that is 100% native american ( or african or whatever) both outside than inside.<br /> Actually, I'm proud of my heritage, as every person should be, and it's exaclty because I highly respect every culture and ethnicity I know about, that I feel wrong to play a 100% ethnic wendigo.<br /> And that's why I would allow and I would play a ''white'' wendigo, for ''white'' ( or also black or whatever) I mean a wendigo with distant native ancestors:<br /> <br /> 1- Because I understand that someone can feel wrong, and feels that he's ''stealing'' culture.<br /> 2- Because actually, it's the totem that can allow you to join the tribe, even if your Native ancestor is four or five generations behind you.<br /> 3- I like to think about an ''eurosiberian'' culture of Wendigo that are able to cooperate with other tribes<br /> 4- I see no problems in a mature game to play a white or black wendigo that can have problem with his tribesmate because he looks everything but not native american.<br /> 5- Political Incorrectness is one of the best thing of werewolf. I like to face ethnic feuds with mature people during a game session.<br /> 6 - it's not because ''I don't want to have dark skin''. Actually, I feel wrong into play a dark skin character because, as I said, I feel that I'm disrespecting someone else cultural heritage to play something too far away from me.</div> </div> </div> </div>First I want to start with, I'm not against people being proud of their heritage. And I apologize if my post makes it sound like I was calling you racist. A lot of that post is based on my past experience with people playing Wendigo, and probably being exposed too much to the Cordell Walkers and Ray Levoi's of pop culture. I swear topic would be much easier to discuss in person. <br /> <br /> So much of the Wendigo tribal identity was wrapped around First Nations cultures. If you're transplanting the Wendigo into Europe then having generations go by where they are surrounded by Europeans and intermarried with white kin folk, it makes me wonder, why play as a Wendigo? Since you bring up a concern about playing other people's culture, would these Wendigo be very European in culture? What cultural traits will these Garou have that would make the totem still want to pick them? Why wouldn't they end up with the Fenrir or Furies instead? These are genuine questions i'm curious about, so if I sound preachy, that's not my goal.<br /> <br /> Also as a side note, personally I don't feel its wrong to play another culture in an RPG. If anything I see it as an opportunity to research that other cultures, and learn more about other people. Its not like you're going to be raking in cash and fame at the expense of other people over this. I can understand if you don't feel comfortable, and I get that. Gaming is meant to be fun. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T17:49:28-08:00","id":1186134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186047#post1186047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying you can't have mixed race Wendigo who aren't Adam Beach look a likes. Like with my own family, I've grown up getting the odd looks when we introduce each other new people, and have been treated differently by people as well. For me being a Wendigo more about sticking tightly to both the Wendigo tribal culture as well as that of the kin culture you came from. Trying to maintain your people's identity despite all the hardships that both have faced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I didn't mean to sound like I was coming after you. I meant to directly address your quote and then went off on a general tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186039#post1186039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My games have/had something similar, an ... I think alliance is too strong of a word, more like &quot;mutual understanding&quot;, between the Three Brothers, the Three Sisters (as I tend to refer to the American Bastet tribes), Nuwisha, and Gurahl, Corax, and Camazotz, and the more openminded Mokole. Sadly, it was badly crippled by the lost of the Croatan and all but lost in the second War of Rage, but started to make signs of a comeback in the 70s and 80s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of how I pictured it too. There was an understanding, and cooperation over major things, but not running around in formalized multi-fera packs like with the Hengoyaki.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186039#post1186039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for South American Garou, there are a few mentions of native Uktena in Rage Across the Amazon and A World of Rage, IIRC, but not much else. I think the biggest issue is the lack of wolves in South America, but given the Uktena's propensity for learning secrets, I don't think it's that far fetched for them to have learned the secret of breeding with maned wolves (which is apparently not wolf, coyote, fox, dog or jackal, but it's own unique thing) the same way the Bunyip adapted to Australia and the one branch of Red Talons did to Southern Africa.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I had no idea such an animal existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-14-2018, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T17:59:45-08:00","id":1186140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186134#post1186134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry. I didn't mean to sound like I was coming after you. I meant to directly address your quote and then went off on a general tangent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I actually worried I was being misunderstood (as can happen on these forums). There was the talk about how something feels off about Euro-Wendigo. I was adding for me, why I'm not a big fan and was curious as to how alone I was in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 02-14-2018, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T00:01:52-08:00","id":1186200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186047#post1186047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First I want to start with, I'm not against people being proud of their heritage. And I apologize if my post makes it sound like I was calling you racist. A lot of that post is based on my past experience with people playing Wendigo, and probably being exposed too much to the Cordell Walkers and Ray Levoi's of pop culture. I swear topic would be much easier to discuss in person.<br /> <br /> So much of the Wendigo tribal identity was wrapped around First Nations cultures. If you're transplanting the Wendigo into Europe then having generations go by where they are surrounded by Europeans and intermarried with white kin folk, it makes me wonder, why play as a Wendigo? Since you bring up a concern about playing other people's culture, would these Wendigo be very European in culture? What cultural traits will these Garou have that would make the totem still want to pick them? Why wouldn't they end up with the Fenrir or Furies instead? These are genuine questions i'm curious about, so if I sound preachy, that's not my goal.<br /> <br /> Also as a side note, personally I don't feel its wrong to play another culture in an RPG. If anything I see it as an opportunity to research that other cultures, and learn more about other people. Its not like you're going to be raking in cash and fame at the expense of other people over this. I can understand if you don't feel comfortable, and I get that. Gaming is meant to be fun.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely no offense taken my friend, absolutely, I was just trying to clarify why I don't feel 100% ok to play a full blood native.<br /> By the way your questions are all fair points, let me try to explain what I would allow and what I would not:<br /> If I will allow people to play as ''euro'' wendigo, I'll allow only characters ( even white in appaearance) that have some yakut, sami, siberian ancestors even far from their generation: but of course, I will never allow a character to become a wendigo even if he's 25% siberian/sami/yakut or whatever if he's growed up in an european sept. What I mean is that geographical location is not an option: even if he was born white with far wendigo ancestors, he needs to shift near a ''wendigo cultural'' zone, so, northern scandinavia/finland, russia or somewhere in the middle of the steppe or siberia: he needs to know the local culture. Or maybe, even if he's from a mediterranean place, he need to shift into an appropriate geographical zone, and probably the tribe will force him to join them, if the totem wants him ( I'm skeptical about this option but it's just an example).<br /> In other words: the character will never be 100% european in culture and way of life. <br /> <br /> You know, I think is something like a ''cultural problem''. My best friend is an adopted guy from southern america and he's clearly a native. When I talk with him I feel that my culture is really far away from his history and culture. So basically, I really feel wrong to play something that has 0% in common with my heritage, culturally and ethnically.<br /> And this not because I dislike what he says, but because I really respect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:30:23-08:00","id":1186470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186200#post1186200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I will allow people to play as ''euro'' wendigo, I'll allow only characters ( even white in appaearance) that have some yakut, sami, siberian ancestors even far from their generation: but of course, I will never allow a character to become a wendigo even if he's 25% siberian/sami/yakut or whatever if he's growed up in an european sept. What I mean is that geographical location is not an option: even if he was born white with far wendigo ancestors, he needs to shift near a ''wendigo cultural'' zone, so, northern scandinavia/finland, russia or somewhere in the middle of the steppe or siberia: he needs to know the local culture. Or maybe, even if he's from a mediterranean place, he need to shift into an appropriate geographical zone, and probably the tribe will force him to join them, if the totem wants him ( I'm skeptical about this option but it's just an example).<br /> In other words: the character will never be 100% european in culture and way of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>So from what I'm reading this is a part of that &quot;Blonde in Buckskin&quot; trope. Maybe being out in Italy its not a common thing to run into, but in American pop culture its rather common to have films. It something I've been over exposed to, which resulted in my feelings on the topic. Being out in Italy it may not be as common of a thing, I'm not sure. The trope centers around a white protagonist with some ancestry somewhere back (if at all), who is taken in by native people and take the culture on as their own.<br /> <br /> BNS seems like it may end up changing what that tribe is about a lot. After reading your post though, if you don't want to play a culture that's not your own, I'm curious...what about the Wendigo makes you want to play one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 02-15-2018, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:12:43-08:00","id":1186839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1185057-wendigo-technical-problem?p=1186134#post1186134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of how I pictured it too. There was an understanding, and cooperation over major things, but not running around in formalized multi-fera packs like with the Hengoyaki.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I had no idea such an animal existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured that back in the &quot;Pure Lands&quot; period, even packs of mixed Uktena, Croatan and/or Wendigo were fairly rare, let alone something like a Corax following a group around or what not. <br /> <br /> And yeah, the maned wolf is kind of weird. Aside from looking a bit like a coyote someone stuck with a hyena haircut and a set of stilts, for the longest time IIRC they were believed to be a type of fox, and it's only in the past decade or so that they've been recognized as &quot;something else&quot;. I, personally, am rather happy with this development, as it just makes my long running house rule that, &quot;yes, there are Garou in South America (mostly in the southern half)&quot; work better. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:30:32-08:00","id":1191664,"title":"","content":"My feeling is that Kinfolk have to be looked at closely. My feeling is that Kinfolk are not the determining factor of whether a lost cub will emerge but the Changers they mate. In my opinion, the Asian Kin of the Three Brothers may have isolated valleys where because of limited breeding with outside world would breed True Wendigo, Uktena, and Croatan. But when the Brothers left for the New World any Kinfolk left behind would be claimed by Hakken Shadow Lords and Stargazers as well as the Fera of the Beast Courts. This means a Croatan Kinfolk wolf that breeds with a Hakken is now a line of Shadow Lords and the future generations are tied to Shadow Lords. Like wise when a Khan breeds with a lost Wendigo human Kinfolk the future line is bred as Khan not Garou. Likewise when Buffalo Bill's Wild West Show visited England Bounces-on-Buffalo, Wendigo Ragabash, had a tryst with a Fianna Kinfolk in London. There is now a Wendio bloodline in England. But any Wendigo breeding true is cut off from their tribe, and the Great Wendigo has long left the Old World. Such Lost Cubs may end up get adopted by other tribes. <br /> <br /> Now in any post WWII stories, as world travel begins to drop to hours from weeks and months Wendigo and Uktena could travel to England and settle in a small Wales community and join the local Sept. They could Earth Guides, Scouts of the Uktena looking spread word of their beliefs, or perhaps a Sacred Hoop member of the Wendigo. Now a days if Wendigo leaves the America and settle in the Old World they have the option of flying their offspring home to learn of the Wendigo ways. Such young may choose to return to Europe.<br /> <br /> But one question remains in Asia is the Great Wendigo active or Noble Sasquatch favoring the lost cubs of Youngest Brother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7258-black-ushkar","name":"Black Ushkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}